# Where this sits in HSO's portfolio

ERP Unite doesn't replace anything HSO already sells. It extends what HSO already does, and gives sellers something to lead with.

<div class="cols two">
<div class="card">

### **Adjacent to D365 Finance**
Unite integrates with D365 deeply — handoffs, journal posting, master data sync. Where HSO sells D365 today, Unite is the insurance-specific layer that makes it relevant.

</div>
<div class="card">

### **Adjacent to Power Platform**
Unite's AI mapping is a reference architecture for AI-augmented finance workflows. HSO's Power Platform practice gets a concrete artifact to point at.

</div>
</div>

<div class="cols two">
<div class="card">

### **A wedge for the insurance vertical**
HSO already serves financial services. Unite is the conversation-opener that turns a brokerage from a generic D365 customer into an insurance-vertical case study.

</div>
<div class="card">

### **A product, not a project**
The codebase exists. The integrations are wired. HSO inherits a deliverable, not an idea — which means the GTM motion can start in weeks.

</div>
