# Investment + cost shape

What HSO is buying. What customers will pay.

---

# HSO's investment trajectory

What the program costs HSO between today and a sellable product.

- **Phase 1 (now):** infrastructure deploy — days of effort
- **Phase 2 (weeks):** DevOps move — days of effort, low risk
- **Phase 3 (months):** productization — multi-week sprint after mgmt alignment; primary investment
- **Phase 4 (parallel):** PII scrub — compliance-led, scope-dependent
- **Ongoing:** weekly upstream sync with OneDigital — light overhead
- **AI roadmap:** scoped after Phase 3 — incremental investment per feature

*Net: most of HSO's investment is Phase 3. Sizing depends on the locked scope from the alignment meeting.*

---

# Customer cost shape (estimated)

The TCO conversation for a brokerage of typical scale.

| Layer | Annual cost shape | Notes |
|-------|-------------------|-------|
| Azure (App Services, SQL, Functions, Storage) | $30k–$80k | Dev/UAT/Prod across environments; scales with transaction volume |
| Microsoft Entra (External ID for producers) | $5k–$20k | Per-user pricing; producer count drives this |
| Telerik license | $5k–$10k | One-time per developer or annual enterprise |
| Google Gemini inference | $2k–$15k | Volume-dependent; mostly statement mapping |
| Application Gateway + WAF | $5k–$10k | One per environment |
| **Subtotal — direct Azure / vendor** | **$45k–$135k** | Per customer per year |
| HSO professional services | Per engagement | Implementation, integration, customization |
| HSO product license | TBD by commercial mtg | The new HSO revenue line |

*Net: a brokerage already spending six figures annually on back-office headcount sees a clear ROI conversation.*

